1
00:00:53,059 --> 00:00:56,071
[Episode 5. I Love All These Stars]

2
00:01:13,652 --> 00:01:15,545
Are you crazy?

3
00:01:18,558 --> 00:01:20,152
Oh, well...

4
00:01:20,826 --> 00:01:22,691
That went better than I expected.

5
00:01:22,691 --> 00:01:25,372
I thought you'd punch me.

6
00:01:25,372 --> 00:01:26,991
If I were, I'd have kissed you.

7
00:01:26,991 --> 00:01:28,834
I wouldn't ask so nicely.

8
00:01:28,834 --> 00:01:32,963
Some gentleman you are.

9
00:01:32,963 --> 00:01:34,860
Try that on someone who likes it.

10
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:36,300
I can't stand it.

11
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:39,011
How do you know? Never tried it.

12
00:01:39,011 --> 00:01:40,780
Never tried what?

13
00:01:42,301 --> 00:01:43,348
Ki...

14
00:01:43,348 --> 00:01:45,005
Kissing?

15
00:01:46,518 --> 00:01:49,980
I don't know why I'm even telling you this,

16
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:52,691
but I've dated before.

17
00:01:52,691 --> 00:01:54,902
Plenty, actually.

18
00:01:54,902 --> 00:01:56,320
Yeah?

19
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:59,156
What kind of guys?

20
00:01:59,156 --> 00:02:02,451
Music lovers, obviously.

21
00:02:02,451 --> 00:02:04,311
They were all artists.

22
00:02:04,311 --> 00:02:06,391
Artists.

23
00:02:07,164 --> 00:02:09,337
So, broke and unemployed.

24
00:02:09,337 --> 00:02:12,920
And what amazing women have you dated?

25
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:17,633
I bet they were all after your money.

26
00:02:17,633 --> 00:02:18,759
Probably.

27
00:02:18,759 --> 00:02:20,052
<i>What?</i>

28
00:02:20,052 --> 00:02:23,388
<i>Why agree? Now I look stupid.</i>

29
00:02:23,388 --> 00:02:25,235
But you took my money, too.

30
00:02:25,235 --> 00:02:27,908
So you come when I call.

31
00:02:30,813 --> 00:02:32,547
Come in tomorrow.

32
00:02:34,661 --> 00:02:37,236
You'd say that while I'm nursing my dad?

33
00:02:37,236 --> 00:02:40,306
What a heartless slave driver.

34
00:02:40,306 --> 00:02:41,573
Forget it.

35
00:02:41,573 --> 00:02:44,418
I can't work this weekend.

36
00:02:44,418 --> 00:02:45,844
Seriously...

37
00:03:09,155 --> 00:03:11,381
<i>Then can I kiss you?</i>

38
00:03:13,136 --> 00:03:16,549
<i>Why are you doing this to me?</i>

39
00:03:41,258 --> 00:03:45,869
If we'd kissed and I'd felt nothing,

40
00:03:45,869 --> 00:03:48,582
at least I'd know for sure.

41
00:03:48,582 --> 00:03:51,055
[Seheon Hospital]

42
00:04:01,953 --> 00:04:03,751
I'll do it.

43
00:04:21,965 --> 00:04:23,814
<i>Lee Eun Chae?</i>

44
00:04:35,528 --> 00:04:36,921
Sir.

45
00:04:37,565 --> 00:04:39,095
Right here.

46
00:04:41,026 --> 00:04:44,748
Sorry, I have to take this call.

47
00:04:46,387 --> 00:04:47,851
Sorry?

48
00:04:53,522 --> 00:04:55,540
It's good, right?

49
00:04:55,540 --> 00:04:57,800
Yes, it's delicious.

50
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:00,170
When's your next show?

51
00:05:00,170 --> 00:05:01,672
I loved it.

52
00:05:01,672 --> 00:05:05,425
We play in Hongdae every Wednesday.

53
00:05:05,425 --> 00:05:07,132
Oh, yeah?

54
00:05:08,470 --> 00:05:10,176
I should come by.

55
00:05:10,176 --> 00:05:11,779
Please do.

56
00:05:11,779 --> 00:05:12,808
I will.

57
00:05:12,808 --> 00:05:14,397
I'll even bring flowers.

58
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:16,019
Promise?

59
00:05:16,019 --> 00:05:17,668
I promise.

60
00:05:19,458 --> 00:05:21,284
Eat up.

61
00:05:29,514 --> 00:05:33,954
That guy's a doctor here?

62
00:05:33,954 --> 00:05:36,585
She said she was nursing her dad.

63
00:05:36,585 --> 00:05:39,107
But she's on a date.

64
00:05:48,677 --> 00:05:50,721
<i>Where are you?</i>

65
00:05:50,721 --> 00:05:53,280
<i>Taking good care of him?</i>

66
00:05:54,057 --> 00:05:57,452
I wasn't hungry at all earlier,

67
00:05:57,452 --> 00:05:59,727
but it's so good...

68
00:06:04,096 --> 00:06:05,398
[Mr. Park]

69
00:06:08,613 --> 00:06:10,031
Yes.

70
00:06:11,450 --> 00:06:13,323
Got it.

71
00:06:14,510 --> 00:06:16,263
[MRI/CT Check-In]
[Male, Kwon Tae Woong]

72
00:06:16,997 --> 00:06:21,209
We'll run a CT, MRI, and bone scan.

73
00:06:21,209 --> 00:06:23,683
It'll take a while.

74
00:06:36,433 --> 00:06:38,560
It'll take time.

75
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:41,026
Let's wait here.

76
00:06:55,667 --> 00:06:57,350
[Radiology]
[Exam in Progress: Lee Man Deok]

77
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:00,618
Still not done?

78
00:07:08,713 --> 00:07:10,253
Oh, my...

79
00:07:11,885 --> 00:07:14,721
What are you doing here?

80
00:07:14,721 --> 00:07:16,444
And you?

81
00:07:16,444 --> 00:07:19,650
I'm waiting for my dad's tests.

82
00:07:21,186 --> 00:07:22,684
Oh, right.

83
00:07:24,272 --> 00:07:27,717
You're Seheon Group's son, right?

84
00:07:27,717 --> 00:07:29,094
Why not tell me?

85
00:07:29,094 --> 00:07:31,363
Why? Would you fall for me?

86
00:07:31,363 --> 00:07:32,739
Oh, please.

87
00:07:32,739 --> 00:07:36,692
Why haven't you answered my text?

88
00:07:39,121 --> 00:07:40,205
Can't you see?

89
00:07:40,205 --> 00:07:43,309
I've got plenty to do at the hospital.

90
00:07:43,309 --> 00:07:44,425
Yeah.

91
00:07:44,425 --> 00:07:47,298
You certainly looked busy.

92
00:07:47,298 --> 00:07:49,005
What's with that tone?

93
00:07:49,005 --> 00:07:50,841
What? What's wrong with it?

94
00:07:50,841 --> 00:07:52,524
It's weird.

95
00:07:57,889 --> 00:07:59,516
Who are you?

96
00:08:00,851 --> 00:08:02,579
Dad, he is...

97
00:08:02,579 --> 00:08:03,615
"Dad?"

98
00:08:03,615 --> 00:08:05,772
Manager Kwon.

99
00:08:05,772 --> 00:08:07,899
Sir. This is my dad.

100
00:08:07,899 --> 00:08:09,568
Hello, sir.

101
00:08:09,568 --> 00:08:12,028
Oh, Manager Kwon!

102
00:08:12,028 --> 00:08:14,948
We've talked on the phone.

103
00:08:14,948 --> 00:08:16,491
- But...
- Right.

104
00:08:16,491 --> 00:08:17,684
What brings you here?

105
00:08:17,684 --> 00:08:22,254
Well, his father has a checkup today.

106
00:08:23,039 --> 00:08:24,708
What a coincidence!

107
00:08:24,708 --> 00:08:30,180
Then I'll wait and say hello to him. Right?

108
00:08:30,180 --> 00:08:32,382
He has several tests. It'll take hours.

109
00:08:32,382 --> 00:08:34,342
I'll take you upstairs.

110
00:08:34,342 --> 00:08:36,178
I can wait.

111
00:08:36,178 --> 00:08:38,615
- I'd love to say hello.
- That's okay.

112
00:08:39,264 --> 00:08:41,391
There's really no need...

113
00:08:41,391 --> 00:08:42,893
One, two, three!

114
00:08:42,893 --> 00:08:44,477
- Be careful.
- Got you.

115
00:08:44,477 --> 00:08:47,263
- I'm fine.
- Oh, Dad.

116
00:08:53,226 --> 00:08:54,600
Manager Kwon.

117
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:55,653
Yes.

118
00:08:55,653 --> 00:08:58,233
Look after Eun Chae, please.

119
00:08:59,201 --> 00:09:02,662
After I lost their mother,

120
00:09:02,662 --> 00:09:05,737
raising these girls alone...

121
00:09:05,737 --> 00:09:06,750
Dad!

122
00:09:06,750 --> 00:09:09,377
Why bring up something so personal?

123
00:09:09,377 --> 00:09:13,392
My oldest daughter was always so bright.

124
00:09:13,392 --> 00:09:16,968
She started working early.

125
00:09:16,968 --> 00:09:18,470
Congratulations.

126
00:09:18,470 --> 00:09:22,015
If this one can just settle down,

127
00:09:22,015 --> 00:09:24,316
that's all I want.

128
00:09:29,236 --> 00:09:30,398
Hello?

129
00:09:30,398 --> 00:09:32,067
<i>Need anything?</i>

130
00:09:32,067 --> 00:09:33,526
No.

131
00:09:33,526 --> 00:09:35,635
<i>I'm at the hospital. Coming up now.</i>

132
00:09:35,635 --> 00:09:37,692
Really? Right now?

133
00:09:38,657 --> 00:09:42,151
Take your time. Please.

134
00:09:42,151 --> 00:09:43,632
Okay.

135
00:09:45,548 --> 00:09:46,873
Sir.

136
00:09:46,873 --> 00:09:49,292
Shouldn't we go get your father now?

137
00:09:49,292 --> 00:09:50,780
Why?

138
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:52,475
Eun Seo...

139
00:09:53,330 --> 00:09:55,401
Sir,

140
00:09:55,401 --> 00:09:58,716
I hope your surgery goes well. Get well soon.

141
00:09:58,716 --> 00:09:59,719
Oh, yeah.

142
00:09:59,719 --> 00:10:00,856
Thank you.

143
00:10:25,591 --> 00:10:26,625
- My back...
- Dad.

144
00:10:26,625 --> 00:10:27,919
Father.

145
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:30,709
Where's Eun Chae?

146
00:10:30,709 --> 00:10:32,623
Didn't see her?

147
00:10:32,623 --> 00:10:36,363
She just went to see
Manager Kwon from work out.

148
00:10:36,363 --> 00:10:37,590
"Manager Kwon?"

149
00:10:37,590 --> 00:10:39,630
The one with three kids?

150
00:10:51,834 --> 00:10:53,030
[Eun Seo]

151
00:11:33,261 --> 00:11:35,315
No answer.

152
00:11:35,315 --> 00:11:37,588
She'll be here soon.

153
00:11:46,493 --> 00:11:48,180
- What?
- Nothing.

154
00:11:50,387 --> 00:11:52,133
Stop joking around.

155
00:12:00,673 --> 00:12:02,585
You should go.

156
00:12:13,486 --> 00:12:15,495
It's hot.

157
00:12:17,065 --> 00:12:20,693
Avoid anything too strenuous for now.

158
00:12:20,693 --> 00:12:24,320
And we'll monitor you regularly...

159
00:12:26,832 --> 00:12:28,451
I'll see you next time.

160
00:12:28,451 --> 00:12:30,145
Thank you.

161
00:12:33,665 --> 00:12:35,521
Are you okay?

162
00:12:36,455 --> 00:12:37,502
Yes.

163
00:12:37,502 --> 00:12:40,255
The tests went fine.

164
00:12:40,255 --> 00:12:41,888
Let's go.

165
00:13:00,859 --> 00:13:04,203
<i>Did the chairman's checkup go okay?</i>

166
00:13:08,450 --> 00:13:12,007
<i>Why did you ask where I was earlier?</i>

167
00:13:16,871 --> 00:13:19,544
Are you really seeing someone?

168
00:13:19,544 --> 00:13:20,587
Why?

169
00:13:20,587 --> 00:13:22,130
Am I not allowed to?

170
00:13:22,130 --> 00:13:24,104
End it before the rumors start.

171
00:13:24,104 --> 00:13:25,300
No.

172
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:27,927
I'd rather choose my own woman.

173
00:13:27,927 --> 00:13:30,054
Not one you pick for me.

174
00:13:30,054 --> 00:13:31,813
Want to die?

175
00:13:36,728 --> 00:13:38,450
Pull over.

176
00:13:40,621 --> 00:13:42,417
Pull over!

177
00:13:51,534 --> 00:13:53,766
I'm warning you.

178
00:13:53,766 --> 00:13:56,041
End it within three days.

179
00:14:03,129 --> 00:14:04,896
I won't.

180
00:14:10,887 --> 00:14:12,972
Find out if he's seeing anyone.

181
00:14:12,972 --> 00:14:14,470
Yes, sir.

182
00:14:26,437 --> 00:14:28,810
<i>Why aren't you answering?</i>

183
00:14:37,786 --> 00:14:42,519
<i>Thanks to your badly timed text,
you're now the woman I'm dating.</i>

184
00:14:42,519 --> 00:14:44,921
<i>You brought this on yourself.</i>

185
00:14:44,921 --> 00:14:46,999
What's he on about?

186
00:14:53,576 --> 00:14:55,139
What are you talking about?

187
00:14:55,139 --> 00:14:57,501
My father asked who you were.

188
00:14:57,501 --> 00:14:59,435
I said you were my girlfriend.

189
00:14:59,435 --> 00:15:00,867
<i>Are you crazy?</i>

190
00:15:00,867 --> 00:15:02,861
Why would you lie?

191
00:15:02,861 --> 00:15:05,858
Since when am I your girlfriend?

192
00:15:05,858 --> 00:15:07,135
I hate losing.

193
00:15:07,135 --> 00:15:10,543
So you used me to win an argument?

194
00:15:12,244 --> 00:15:15,118
Wait. Your dad's the chairman.

195
00:15:15,118 --> 00:15:16,696
<i>Your father...</i>

196
00:15:16,696 --> 00:15:18,450
<i>Is he scary?</i>

197
00:15:18,450 --> 00:15:19,491
Why?

198
00:15:19,491 --> 00:15:22,625
Because I'm afraid he'll come after me!

199
00:15:22,625 --> 00:15:26,765
Why drag me into your stupid pride contest?

200
00:15:27,425 --> 00:15:29,734
What a weirdo.

201
00:15:29,734 --> 00:15:31,120
I'm hanging up!

202
00:15:34,387 --> 00:15:38,678
Is being my girlfriend really that awful?

203
00:15:54,949 --> 00:15:57,310
Hold on.

204
00:15:57,310 --> 00:15:58,812
Yes?

205
00:16:00,096 --> 00:16:02,498
Eun Seo,

206
00:16:02,498 --> 00:16:06,527
look after Eun Chae when I'm gone.

207
00:16:08,296 --> 00:16:09,547
Jin Woo.

208
00:16:09,547 --> 00:16:11,215
Yes?

209
00:16:11,215 --> 00:16:14,719
Please take care of Eun Seo and Eun Chae.

210
00:16:14,719 --> 00:16:15,720
Of course.

211
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:18,598
Why are you talking like you're dying?

212
00:16:18,598 --> 00:16:21,100
Why not look at Mom's photo one more time?

213
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:22,769
Hey.

214
00:16:22,769 --> 00:16:25,156
Even when I'm gone,

215
00:16:25,156 --> 00:16:27,914
you'd better keep your curfew.

216
00:16:27,914 --> 00:16:29,442
Jeez...

217
00:16:29,442 --> 00:16:32,403
Even if this is our last goodbye,

218
00:16:32,403 --> 00:16:34,989
you're still on about my curfew?

219
00:16:34,989 --> 00:16:36,149
Jin Woo.

220
00:16:36,149 --> 00:16:37,242
Yes?

221
00:16:37,242 --> 00:16:41,641
If she breaks curfew, shave her head for me.

222
00:16:41,641 --> 00:16:43,956
You can do that yourself, Dad.

223
00:16:43,956 --> 00:16:45,503
So I brought this.

224
00:16:45,503 --> 00:16:46,534
What?

225
00:16:47,154 --> 00:16:48,670
Ta-da!

226
00:16:48,670 --> 00:16:52,407
I almost ran late getting this talisman.

227
00:16:52,407 --> 00:16:57,220
You're a criminal psychologist.
You believe in superstitions?

228
00:16:57,220 --> 00:17:01,015
Work enough criminal cases,

229
00:17:01,015 --> 00:17:04,686
and you learn to play it safe.

230
00:17:04,686 --> 00:17:05,978
Oh, come on.

231
00:17:05,978 --> 00:17:07,313
Anyway...

232
00:17:07,313 --> 00:17:09,482
How can he take that into surgery?

233
00:17:09,482 --> 00:17:11,306
Here.

234
00:17:11,306 --> 00:17:12,788
Stick it on.

235
00:17:14,654 --> 00:17:15,697
There?

236
00:17:15,697 --> 00:17:17,031
Done!

237
00:17:17,031 --> 00:17:20,451
I actually feel better already.

238
00:17:20,451 --> 00:17:22,495
- Good luck, Dad.
- Yeah.

239
00:17:22,495 --> 00:17:24,370
Here I go.

240
00:17:28,540 --> 00:17:30,611
We're taking the patient in now.

241
00:17:30,611 --> 00:17:32,376
You got this!

242
00:17:32,376 --> 00:17:34,269
[Lee Man Deok, 60]
[Lumbar Disc Herniation]

243
00:17:39,315 --> 00:17:41,364
I miss Mom.

244
00:17:42,223 --> 00:17:45,699
I used to sing to her in the hospital.

245
00:17:46,315 --> 00:17:50,562
Then make Mom proud. Get a real job.

246
00:17:50,562 --> 00:17:54,318
How much longer must Dad
worry about your curfew?

247
00:17:54,318 --> 00:17:55,528
Beats me.

248
00:17:55,528 --> 00:17:57,316
There you go again.

249
00:17:59,198 --> 00:18:03,286
Mom wouldn't have cared about that.

250
00:18:03,286 --> 00:18:04,683
What?

251
00:18:04,683 --> 00:18:05,719
Hey!

252
00:18:05,719 --> 00:18:07,691
I took you to class while Mom was sick.

253
00:18:07,691 --> 00:18:09,187
Know how hard that was?

254
00:18:09,187 --> 00:18:12,178
I sacrificed plenty for you.

255
00:18:12,178 --> 00:18:14,172
What did you sacrifice?

256
00:18:14,172 --> 00:18:15,505
I hated math.

257
00:18:15,505 --> 00:18:17,825
But you signed up for math tutoring,

258
00:18:17,825 --> 00:18:19,761
so Dad made me go, too.

259
00:18:19,761 --> 00:18:21,721
You still need to grow up...

260
00:18:21,721 --> 00:18:23,558
Enough!

261
00:18:24,682 --> 00:18:28,178
This is why I need to stay healthy.

262
00:18:28,835 --> 00:18:32,638
Is that how two career women should act?

263
00:18:33,421 --> 00:18:34,854
Are you okay?

264
00:18:34,854 --> 00:18:36,736
- Yeah.
- Dad, you okay?

265
00:18:36,736 --> 00:18:38,741
I'm fine.

266
00:18:47,830 --> 00:18:50,316
She just yells at me.

267
00:19:11,479 --> 00:19:12,983
Forget it.

268
00:19:13,564 --> 00:19:14,941
Forget it.

269
00:19:14,941 --> 00:19:16,400
What's it to me?

270
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:18,730
Just win the bet.

271
00:19:19,569 --> 00:19:20,738
Jin.

272
00:19:20,738 --> 00:19:22,824
We need to pick up the pace.

273
00:19:22,824 --> 00:19:24,492
<i>Why? Did something happen?</i>

274
00:19:24,492 --> 00:19:26,531
<i>You don't look happy.</i>

275
00:19:26,531 --> 00:19:27,537
No.

276
00:19:27,537 --> 00:19:28,880
I just...

277
00:19:30,058 --> 00:19:31,624
I just want

278
00:19:31,624 --> 00:19:34,025
to finish up and go back.

279
00:19:38,035 --> 00:19:39,693
The surgery went well.

280
00:19:39,693 --> 00:19:42,348
Why keep staring at that album?

281
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:43,455
Dad.

282
00:19:43,455 --> 00:19:47,098
I told you to remarry
instead of staring at Mom's photo.

283
00:19:47,098 --> 00:19:49,058
Dad, you're in your prime.

284
00:19:49,058 --> 00:19:50,184
Oh, you...

285
00:19:50,184 --> 00:19:51,769
What am I, prime rib?

286
00:19:51,769 --> 00:19:53,354
Am I on the market now?

287
00:19:53,354 --> 00:19:55,022
You rascal.

288
00:19:55,022 --> 00:19:57,427
You're not fighting, are you?

289
00:19:57,427 --> 00:19:58,609
No...

290
00:19:58,609 --> 00:20:00,027
Anyway...

291
00:20:00,027 --> 00:20:02,196
I need some rest now.

292
00:20:02,196 --> 00:20:04,949
You should get going.

293
00:20:04,949 --> 00:20:06,115
I'm staying.

294
00:20:06,115 --> 00:20:08,362
I just got here with milk.

295
00:20:11,247 --> 00:20:13,124
Why don't you take a walk

296
00:20:13,124 --> 00:20:14,901
while your father rests?

297
00:20:14,901 --> 00:20:17,661
But I need to look after him.

298
00:20:20,506 --> 00:20:22,486
Why are you poking me?

299
00:20:22,486 --> 00:20:23,885
Go on!

300
00:20:23,885 --> 00:20:26,220
With the doctor...

301
00:20:26,220 --> 00:20:27,638
He's busy!

302
00:20:27,638 --> 00:20:29,974
He's too busy for me.

303
00:20:29,974 --> 00:20:31,684
Well...

304
00:20:31,684 --> 00:20:33,731
I've got time.

305
00:20:44,426 --> 00:20:46,799
<i>What's gotten into you?</i>

306
00:20:50,995 --> 00:20:53,587
<i>You already have a doctor son-in-law.</i>

307
00:20:53,587 --> 00:20:55,927
<i>How many do you need?</i>

308
00:21:02,618 --> 00:21:05,829
Your dad's being discharged today?

309
00:21:05,829 --> 00:21:09,263
That's great news. But I'm a little sad...

310
00:21:09,263 --> 00:21:11,809
It was so nice seeing you again.

311
00:21:12,975 --> 00:21:14,894
You can come to our shows.

312
00:21:14,894 --> 00:21:16,554
Then...

313
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:19,967
Could I get your number?

314
00:21:25,701 --> 00:21:27,046
Sure.

315
00:21:28,658 --> 00:21:31,285
<i>Hello. I'm Carol.</i>

316
00:21:31,285 --> 00:21:33,758
<i>Hello. I'm Carol.</i>

317
00:21:33,758 --> 00:21:35,860
<i>Hello. I'm Carol.</i>

318
00:21:35,860 --> 00:21:38,295
<i>Hello. I'm Carol.</i>

319
00:22:26,468 --> 00:22:29,961
She was always loud when she was around...

320
00:22:47,486 --> 00:22:49,805
Eun Chae said she'd be in today.

321
00:22:49,805 --> 00:22:52,659
Shouldn't she be here by now?

322
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:54,452
She'll be here soon.

323
00:22:54,452 --> 00:22:55,536
Let's head in.

324
00:22:55,536 --> 00:22:57,659
Oh, right.

325
00:22:57,659 --> 00:22:58,697
You know...

326
00:22:58,697 --> 00:23:00,995
Is anything bothering you here?

327
00:23:00,995 --> 00:23:02,001
All of a sudden?

328
00:23:02,001 --> 00:23:03,210
Just curious.

329
00:23:03,210 --> 00:23:04,597
Right now.

330
00:23:04,597 --> 00:23:05,629
- What...
- Oh!

331
00:23:05,629 --> 00:23:07,682
There she is.

332
00:23:08,325 --> 00:23:10,619
- Eun Chae.
- Hello, sir.

333
00:23:10,619 --> 00:23:11,719
Your dad's okay, right?

334
00:23:11,719 --> 00:23:12,785
Yes.

335
00:23:13,512 --> 00:23:15,125
- Get to work.
- Yes, sir.

336
00:23:18,768 --> 00:23:20,175
Oh, man.

337
00:23:20,842 --> 00:23:23,689
I forgot my coffee.

338
00:23:23,689 --> 00:23:27,008
I can't work without my coffee.

339
00:23:29,613 --> 00:23:30,696
<i>Yes, Mr. Kwon?</i>

340
00:23:30,696 --> 00:23:31,847
Coffee, please.

341
00:23:31,847 --> 00:23:33,459
<i>Got it.</i>

342
00:23:39,552 --> 00:23:41,499
Use some force.

343
00:23:45,419 --> 00:23:46,905
Yes.

344
00:23:53,284 --> 00:23:56,097
Eun Chae's out on my errand,

345
00:23:56,097 --> 00:23:57,624
so I...

346
00:24:18,959 --> 00:24:20,746
<i>Need anything?</i>

347
00:24:22,748 --> 00:24:26,001
Yes, well...

348
00:24:27,771 --> 00:24:29,761
When's the meeting?

349
00:24:30,506 --> 00:24:32,091
<i>Two this afternoon.</i>

350
00:24:32,091 --> 00:24:33,092
Right.

351
00:24:33,092 --> 00:24:34,884
Got it.

352
00:24:48,858 --> 00:24:51,735
<i>Find out if he's seeing anyone.</i>

353
00:24:51,735 --> 00:24:54,715
But all he thinks about is work.

354
00:25:04,796 --> 00:25:06,742
Have a seat.

355
00:25:10,296 --> 00:25:13,299
What's this about?

356
00:25:13,299 --> 00:25:15,426
Eun Chae...

357
00:25:15,426 --> 00:25:16,844
I...

358
00:25:16,844 --> 00:25:19,009
I was completely wrong.

359
00:25:19,638 --> 00:25:22,057
Out of the blue?

360
00:25:22,057 --> 00:25:24,803
I'm truly sorry.

361
00:25:24,803 --> 00:25:26,187
No, wait.

362
00:25:26,187 --> 00:25:28,939
I'll even get on my knees.

363
00:25:28,939 --> 00:25:31,856
- Oh, my...
- Please... forgive me.

364
00:25:32,943 --> 00:25:34,653
Me, too.

365
00:25:34,653 --> 00:25:36,113
Back then...

366
00:25:36,113 --> 00:25:39,377
I'm sorry I didn't stand up for you.

367
00:25:39,377 --> 00:25:40,409
I was an idiot.

368
00:25:40,409 --> 00:25:43,412
I'll get on my knees, if you want.

369
00:25:43,412 --> 00:25:45,956
Wait, why are you doing this?

370
00:25:45,956 --> 00:25:47,291
Get up!

371
00:25:47,291 --> 00:25:49,129
Come on!

372
00:25:50,878 --> 00:25:52,621
Seriously...

373
00:25:53,172 --> 00:25:55,297
Do you really mean it?

374
00:25:55,297 --> 00:25:56,848
Of course!

375
00:25:57,340 --> 00:26:00,885
I truly, deeply regret it. I swear!

376
00:26:02,556 --> 00:26:06,060
<i>I saw them apologize to Lee Eun Chae.</i>

377
00:26:06,060 --> 00:26:08,262
Good work.

378
00:26:23,202 --> 00:26:25,622
This one's nice.

379
00:26:26,580 --> 00:26:29,820
Jin Woo looks good in cool tones.

380
00:26:29,820 --> 00:26:32,211
This would suit him.

381
00:26:32,211 --> 00:26:33,957
It's pretty.

382
00:26:46,350 --> 00:26:48,283
I like this one.

383
00:27:02,933 --> 00:27:05,327
Shopping?

384
00:27:05,327 --> 00:27:07,454
Didn't you have only 20,000 won?

385
00:27:07,454 --> 00:27:09,999
They're gifts.

386
00:27:09,999 --> 00:27:12,251
First paycheck. Gifts for family.

387
00:27:12,251 --> 00:27:14,153
Not that you'd understand.

388
00:27:15,464 --> 00:27:19,008
<i>Dad, Eun Seo, Jin Woo...</i>

389
00:27:19,008 --> 00:27:21,302
<i>Then who's that one for?</i>

390
00:27:21,302 --> 00:27:22,864
<i>Me?</i>

391
00:27:37,526 --> 00:27:39,017
Already?

392
00:27:39,695 --> 00:27:42,614
Tonight's dinner recommendation is...

393
00:27:42,614 --> 00:27:44,757
You can go home.

394
00:27:45,284 --> 00:27:46,998
For real?

395
00:27:46,998 --> 00:27:49,496
What's gotten into you?

396
00:27:49,496 --> 00:27:50,829
Yes!

397
00:27:56,462 --> 00:27:58,389
I'll go, then.

398
00:27:59,673 --> 00:28:01,862
Really okay to leave?

399
00:28:01,862 --> 00:28:02,885
Yeah.

400
00:28:02,885 --> 00:28:04,386
Go.

401
00:28:07,546 --> 00:28:09,194
Mine...

402
00:28:10,184 --> 00:28:11,800
Where's mine?

403
00:28:16,729 --> 00:28:18,803
There it is.

404
00:28:23,572 --> 00:28:27,326
This one's for Dad.

405
00:28:27,326 --> 00:28:29,043
This is for Eun Seo.

406
00:28:29,043 --> 00:28:31,372
And this is for Jin Woo.

407
00:28:34,291 --> 00:28:35,876
What's wrong?

408
00:28:35,876 --> 00:28:39,129
Are you guys just so happy...

409
00:28:39,129 --> 00:28:40,716
Is that it?

410
00:28:42,049 --> 00:28:44,470
Thanks, Eun Chae, but...

411
00:28:44,470 --> 00:28:48,097
I'm not sure I should accept this.

412
00:28:48,097 --> 00:28:49,554
Is something going on?

413
00:28:49,554 --> 00:28:50,557
Seriously.

414
00:28:50,557 --> 00:28:52,309
Be honest, Eun Chae.

415
00:28:52,309 --> 00:28:53,644
Something's up, isn't it?

416
00:28:53,644 --> 00:28:56,563
Why else would you bring us gifts?

417
00:28:56,563 --> 00:28:58,482
Oh, come on.

418
00:28:58,482 --> 00:29:01,130
Did you study psychology just to grill me?

419
00:29:01,130 --> 00:29:03,987
I've been busy since payday,

420
00:29:03,987 --> 00:29:06,030
so the gifts came late. That's all.

421
00:29:06,030 --> 00:29:07,950
So we can...

422
00:29:07,950 --> 00:29:11,383
just enjoy these, no strings attached?

423
00:29:12,599 --> 00:29:14,468
I told you!

424
00:29:14,957 --> 00:29:17,126
Still feels fishy.

425
00:29:17,126 --> 00:29:19,211
Well, she insisted...

426
00:29:19,211 --> 00:29:20,637
Unboxing time!

427
00:29:20,637 --> 00:29:22,381
- Unboxing!
- Unboxing!

428
00:29:22,381 --> 00:29:23,526
Unboxing!

429
00:29:23,526 --> 00:29:25,132
Oh, my...

430
00:29:25,132 --> 00:29:26,140
Eun Chae!

431
00:29:27,219 --> 00:29:28,979
Yours is nice, too.

432
00:29:31,181 --> 00:29:32,766
Lunch?

433
00:29:32,766 --> 00:29:34,601
And the hospital?

434
00:29:34,601 --> 00:29:36,270
- Near my office?
<i>- Hospital?</i>

435
00:29:36,270 --> 00:29:37,672
<i>That means...</i>

436
00:29:38,814 --> 00:29:41,191
I'm out on work right now.

437
00:29:41,191 --> 00:29:42,307
Then how about...

438
00:29:42,307 --> 00:29:45,797
Firenze nearby, at noon?

439
00:29:46,739 --> 00:29:48,615
I'll text you the address.

440
00:29:48,615 --> 00:29:50,511
See you there.

441
00:29:53,436 --> 00:29:55,405
I missed Italian food.

442
00:30:09,511 --> 00:30:11,773
What am I doing?

443
00:30:11,773 --> 00:30:12,806
No.

444
00:30:12,806 --> 00:30:14,683
No, no.

445
00:30:14,683 --> 00:30:17,926
I came because I wanted pasta, too.

446
00:30:21,106 --> 00:30:23,466
Just bring me your best dish.

447
00:30:23,466 --> 00:30:25,157
Of course.

448
00:30:25,157 --> 00:30:26,417
Oh, right.

449
00:30:26,417 --> 00:30:27,946
I have something for you.

450
00:30:27,946 --> 00:30:29,257
What is it?

451
00:30:29,990 --> 00:30:32,035
Ta-da!

452
00:30:32,035 --> 00:30:33,285
This is for me?

453
00:30:33,285 --> 00:30:34,468
Yes.

454
00:30:35,996 --> 00:30:38,624
I wanted to thank you for last time.

455
00:30:38,624 --> 00:30:41,210
For fixing my shoe,

456
00:30:41,210 --> 00:30:45,350
and the flowers, even if it was an errand.

457
00:30:46,077 --> 00:30:47,429
Really?

458
00:30:48,195 --> 00:30:49,510
Thank you so much!

459
00:30:49,510 --> 00:30:51,905
What a surprise!

460
00:30:51,905 --> 00:30:53,639
Curious what's inside?

461
00:30:53,639 --> 00:30:55,390
Open it when you get home.

462
00:30:55,390 --> 00:30:56,836
I can't wait.

463
00:30:59,228 --> 00:31:01,012
Is something bothering you?

464
00:31:01,012 --> 00:31:03,038
No, I'm fine.

465
00:31:15,606 --> 00:31:17,192
What's wrong?

466
00:31:18,650 --> 00:31:22,582
There's a guy over there
who looks absolutely starving.

467
00:31:22,582 --> 00:31:24,017
Oh, yeah?

468
00:31:26,196 --> 00:31:27,617
Let me see.

469
00:31:32,192 --> 00:31:33,921
He's not here.

470
00:31:33,921 --> 00:31:35,609
He must've left.

471
00:31:36,223 --> 00:31:37,975
Too bad.

472
00:31:37,975 --> 00:31:39,648
I wanted to see him, too.

473
00:31:40,480 --> 00:31:43,121
So that's it.

474
00:31:43,121 --> 00:31:49,033
She said she'd never fall for me
because of that doctor.

475
00:31:53,479 --> 00:31:54,591
Come in.

476
00:32:01,921 --> 00:32:03,622
Did you enjoy your lunch?

477
00:32:03,622 --> 00:32:07,224
Didn't know you cared about that.

478
00:32:07,224 --> 00:32:09,631
I bet you did.

479
00:32:09,631 --> 00:32:13,969
Didn't even think to ask
if your boss had lunch.

480
00:32:13,969 --> 00:32:18,037
You said you weren't hungry earlier.

481
00:32:18,037 --> 00:32:22,561
So you do get cravings.

482
00:32:22,561 --> 00:32:24,214
Want food?

483
00:32:28,984 --> 00:32:30,569
"New OX."

484
00:32:30,569 --> 00:32:33,071
"Full-group comeback planned?"

485
00:32:33,071 --> 00:32:34,450
What?

486
00:32:34,948 --> 00:32:36,658
What's going on here?

487
00:32:36,658 --> 00:32:39,536
Who approved a full-group comeback?

488
00:32:39,536 --> 00:32:43,248
I clearly said to kick out
the member who caused the scandal.

489
00:32:43,248 --> 00:32:44,419
Yes, sir.

490
00:32:44,419 --> 00:32:48,686
But Mrs. Jeong approved it.

491
00:32:50,208 --> 00:32:52,424
And as for New OX's members,

492
00:32:52,424 --> 00:32:56,637
I don't think you should decide
to kick one out on your own.

493
00:32:56,637 --> 00:33:00,098
Who do you think runs this company?

494
00:33:00,098 --> 00:33:04,144
Well, our largest shareholder, Mrs. Jeong...

495
00:33:04,144 --> 00:33:05,594
Wrong.

496
00:33:06,313 --> 00:33:08,619
Seheon Group is the largest shareholder.

497
00:33:08,619 --> 00:33:11,745
And I'm the CEO they appointed.

498
00:33:11,745 --> 00:33:16,093
If you can't accept my decisions, leave.

499
00:33:22,704 --> 00:33:25,708
You said I could pick.

500
00:33:25,708 --> 00:33:29,169
Try it. Spicy food helps with stress.

501
00:33:29,169 --> 00:33:31,463
I can't do spicy.

502
00:33:31,463 --> 00:33:33,026
You can't?

503
00:33:42,574 --> 00:33:45,760
Why are you being so gross?

504
00:33:45,760 --> 00:33:47,082
What's wrong?

505
00:33:48,188 --> 00:33:49,272
What's going on?

506
00:33:49,272 --> 00:33:50,691
You can't eat spicy food.

507
00:33:50,691 --> 00:33:52,830
Try it this way.

508
00:33:52,830 --> 00:33:55,104
- No.
- Just try it.

509
00:33:55,104 --> 00:33:56,305
- Stop...
- Come on!

510
00:33:56,305 --> 00:33:58,073
Just try it!

511
00:33:58,073 --> 00:33:59,597
Don't...

512
00:34:06,167 --> 00:34:08,166
Careful. You'll get sick again.

513
00:34:08,166 --> 00:34:10,460
Want me to prick your finger again?

514
00:34:10,460 --> 00:34:12,693
Enough. Forget it.

515
00:34:13,839 --> 00:34:15,918
Here, read this.

516
00:34:26,230 --> 00:34:27,284
[Expansion Strategy]

517
00:34:27,284 --> 00:34:28,759
[New Trainee Group] [Region-Specific Group]

518
00:34:29,396 --> 00:34:33,454
What if the new groups spun off from New OX

519
00:34:33,454 --> 00:34:36,016
each lived on a different planet?

520
00:34:36,016 --> 00:34:37,988
We could expand their universe.

521
00:34:37,988 --> 00:34:42,117
And each group could be named
after a constellation.

522
00:34:42,117 --> 00:34:45,620
We're all shining stars,

523
00:34:45,620 --> 00:34:48,481
forming our own constellations.

524
00:34:51,501 --> 00:34:53,086
How childish.

525
00:34:53,086 --> 00:34:55,756
The best ideas are cheesy.

526
00:34:55,756 --> 00:34:58,389
Then why bother asking me?

527
00:34:58,389 --> 00:34:59,760
Oh, sorry.

528
00:34:59,760 --> 00:35:02,888
Sometimes I forget people aren't rational.

529
00:35:02,888 --> 00:35:06,333
Being rational isn't always better.

530
00:35:07,809 --> 00:35:09,728
Music...

531
00:35:09,728 --> 00:35:11,700
is like glass.

532
00:35:12,689 --> 00:35:14,480
It catches sunlight,

533
00:35:14,480 --> 00:35:18,820
and looks different from every angle.

534
00:35:18,820 --> 00:35:20,363
Diffuse reflection?

535
00:35:20,363 --> 00:35:23,075
You have zero sense of romance.

536
00:35:24,895 --> 00:35:25,935
But...

537
00:35:25,935 --> 00:35:29,111
<i>Who was that guy you had lunch with?</i>

538
00:35:32,935 --> 00:35:34,158
No.

539
00:35:48,947 --> 00:35:51,067
<i>Boss, are you okay?</i>

540
00:35:55,607 --> 00:35:58,819
Shouldn't you at least ask if I'm okay?

541
00:35:58,819 --> 00:36:01,659
<i>I just did, Boss.</i>

542
00:36:07,004 --> 00:36:09,004
[Lee Eun Chae]

543
00:36:10,588 --> 00:36:12,361
No, no.

544
00:36:13,875 --> 00:36:15,405
Keep it together.

545
00:36:24,149 --> 00:36:26,253
<i>How's your stomach?</i>

546
00:36:26,253 --> 00:36:27,942
<i>Not good.</i>

547
00:36:38,733 --> 00:36:40,235
Wait...

548
00:36:40,235 --> 00:36:42,859
Is she worried about me?

549
00:36:50,078 --> 00:36:51,955
Get a grip.

550
00:36:51,955 --> 00:36:52,956
Don't smile.

551
00:36:52,956 --> 00:36:54,827
If you smile, you lose.

552
00:37:00,881 --> 00:37:03,254
Mr. Kwon.

553
00:37:04,384 --> 00:37:09,174
It's Wednesday. Can I leave at six?

554
00:37:10,849 --> 00:37:13,030
<i>Wednesday again?</i>

555
00:37:14,436 --> 00:37:16,438
Is this going to happen every week?

556
00:37:16,438 --> 00:37:20,775
Can't you spare me overtime once a week?

557
00:37:20,775 --> 00:37:24,687
<i>I have no real reason to stop her.</i>

558
00:37:25,572 --> 00:37:26,615
Then...

559
00:37:26,615 --> 00:37:28,125
I'll take that as a yes.

560
00:37:28,125 --> 00:37:29,701
See you tomorrow.

561
00:37:29,701 --> 00:37:31,967
Sir, you're the best!

562
00:37:40,378 --> 00:37:42,424
The whole club?

563
00:37:43,423 --> 00:37:47,677
They paid in full. Why aren't they here?

564
00:37:47,677 --> 00:37:49,911
This is ridiculous.

565
00:37:50,513 --> 00:37:51,979
Hold on.

566
00:37:53,308 --> 00:37:56,119
It's already nine.

567
00:37:56,784 --> 00:37:59,189
A no-show?

568
00:37:59,189 --> 00:38:01,107
Let's let customers in.

569
00:38:01,107 --> 00:38:04,069
What kind of psycho pays all that money and...

570
00:38:04,069 --> 00:38:05,735
Sorry I'm late.

571
00:38:15,246 --> 00:38:16,289
That guy...

572
00:38:16,289 --> 00:38:19,010
- Wait.
- Why are you here?

573
00:38:24,687 --> 00:38:26,841
You rented out the whole club?

574
00:38:26,841 --> 00:38:29,500
Why else would I be here?

575
00:38:36,777 --> 00:38:39,646
I actually work at his company.

576
00:38:39,646 --> 00:38:40,897
- What?
- What?

577
00:38:40,897 --> 00:38:42,452
- So he's the psychopath...
- Hey!

578
00:38:42,452 --> 00:38:44,508
More importantly,

579
00:38:47,070 --> 00:38:49,570
why did you book here?

580
00:39:00,903 --> 00:39:02,717
OYES Entertainment's CEO?

581
00:39:03,670 --> 00:39:05,672
So that's why you were after Soo...

582
00:39:05,672 --> 00:39:08,258
I'm interested in India Red.

583
00:39:08,258 --> 00:39:09,444
But...

584
00:39:10,218 --> 00:39:12,205
there's one thing.

585
00:39:13,096 --> 00:39:15,932
How about changing Soo's concept?

586
00:39:15,932 --> 00:39:17,892
- What do you mean?
- Absolutely not.

587
00:39:17,892 --> 00:39:20,145
Soo is the face of India Red.

588
00:39:20,145 --> 00:39:23,757
Can't be an icon if nobody knows you.

589
00:39:25,276 --> 00:39:27,663
No present, no future.

590
00:39:29,070 --> 00:39:31,740
You have a chance to sign now.

591
00:39:31,740 --> 00:39:36,430
Do you really need to stick with this concept?

592
00:39:38,065 --> 00:39:40,972
See us play, then decide.

593
00:39:44,799 --> 00:39:48,385
One, two, three, four.

594
00:42:27,942 --> 00:42:29,234
Why?

595
00:42:32,545 --> 00:42:34,047
About Soo...

596
00:42:34,047 --> 00:42:38,331
We're not changing who we are.

597
00:42:40,762 --> 00:42:42,312
That's me,

598
00:42:44,683 --> 00:42:46,992
and that's India Red.

599
00:43:00,281 --> 00:43:01,507
No.

600
00:43:02,075 --> 00:43:05,054
Do Hyeok, what are you thinking?

601
00:43:06,120 --> 00:43:09,257
Just focus on winning the bet.

602
00:43:19,717 --> 00:43:23,012
Resort meeting in Gangwon-do tomorrow.

603
00:43:23,012 --> 00:43:25,742
I'll be out front in the morning.

604
00:43:38,236 --> 00:43:39,279
Lee Eun Chae.

605
00:43:39,279 --> 00:43:40,442
Get in.

606
00:43:43,866 --> 00:43:46,560
What's your angle this time?

607
00:43:50,499 --> 00:43:52,985
- Yes?
- Oh, sir.

608
00:43:52,985 --> 00:43:56,129
I'm waiting outside your home.

609
00:43:56,129 --> 00:43:58,340
I'm taking my assistant today.

610
00:44:00,216 --> 00:44:02,315
Where are we going?

611
00:44:06,084 --> 00:44:07,550
Hey...

612
00:44:08,150 --> 00:44:10,083
Where are we going?

613
00:44:17,942 --> 00:44:21,195
Wow! The ocean!

614
00:44:21,195 --> 00:44:23,156
Can we stop and see the water?

615
00:44:23,156 --> 00:44:25,676
We're not here on vacation.

616
00:44:28,369 --> 00:44:30,453
You're looking at it now.

617
00:44:30,453 --> 00:44:31,456
I mean...

618
00:44:31,456 --> 00:44:35,433
We could stop, take some pictures...

619
00:44:36,544 --> 00:44:38,929
It's so beautiful!

620
00:44:45,932 --> 00:44:48,931
For the building's exterior and upkeep,

621
00:44:48,931 --> 00:44:51,734
please review the additional documents.

622
00:44:52,977 --> 00:44:55,004
And meeting minutes...

623
00:45:00,251 --> 00:45:01,632
Hand it over.

624
00:45:10,716 --> 00:45:14,582
You could've told me we'd be staying overnight.

625
00:45:14,582 --> 00:45:18,383
Why cook? We could just eat out.

626
00:45:19,836 --> 00:45:21,425
Pork belly's on sale!

627
00:45:22,799 --> 00:45:25,285
Here, hold this.

628
00:45:25,885 --> 00:45:27,399
That's so cheap!

629
00:45:45,675 --> 00:45:47,945
Come over here.

630
00:45:49,283 --> 00:45:50,326
No, thanks.

631
00:45:50,326 --> 00:45:51,874
I'm not hungry.

632
00:45:55,415 --> 00:45:56,958
Now...

633
00:45:56,958 --> 00:45:59,244
A perilla leaf...

634
00:45:59,244 --> 00:46:00,913
And this...

635
00:46:08,928 --> 00:46:10,360
This is so good!

636
00:46:10,360 --> 00:46:13,599
Stop talking with your mouth full.

637
00:46:13,599 --> 00:46:15,367
It's gross.

638
00:46:28,865 --> 00:46:32,785
It's annoying how much you enjoy that.

639
00:46:32,785 --> 00:46:34,912
I'm just enjoying my food!

640
00:46:34,912 --> 00:46:37,178
Why does that bother you?

641
00:46:44,172 --> 00:46:48,132
Do you have a knife and fork?

642
00:46:50,428 --> 00:46:55,556
Don't tell me you're cutting off the fat.

643
00:46:56,726 --> 00:46:57,935
Don't eat it!

644
00:46:57,935 --> 00:47:00,980
That's an insult to pork belly.

645
00:47:00,980 --> 00:47:02,273
Fine,

646
00:47:02,273 --> 00:47:03,852
I won't eat it.

647
00:47:07,820 --> 00:47:09,900
Fine. I'll be generous.

648
00:47:12,074 --> 00:47:16,734
I'll make you a wrap using my special recipe.

649
00:47:17,830 --> 00:47:19,794
Ssamjang.

650
00:47:23,127 --> 00:47:26,464
Made it nice and pretty, didn't I?

651
00:47:26,464 --> 00:47:27,507
Here.

652
00:47:29,467 --> 00:47:31,177
Oh, come on.

653
00:47:31,177 --> 00:47:34,096
Just try it!

654
00:47:41,521 --> 00:47:42,939
Chew.

655
00:47:47,610 --> 00:47:49,504
Oh, right. Dad.

656
00:47:54,742 --> 00:47:57,745
Dad, I'm on a business trip.

657
00:47:57,745 --> 00:47:59,460
Back tomorrow.

658
00:48:00,122 --> 00:48:02,542
I'm serious!

659
00:48:02,542 --> 00:48:04,918
I'm with Manager Kwon.

660
00:48:04,918 --> 00:48:06,523
Want him?

661
00:48:12,804 --> 00:48:14,815
So many stars...

662
00:48:14,815 --> 00:48:17,431
There are so many.

663
00:48:17,431 --> 00:48:20,017
I love it.

664
00:48:20,017 --> 00:48:24,843
So many things to love.

665
00:48:25,616 --> 00:48:27,525
You know what?

666
00:48:27,525 --> 00:48:30,194
They say stars twinkle

667
00:48:30,194 --> 00:48:33,501
with all the longing they hold,

668
00:48:33,501 --> 00:48:36,414
shining for one another.

669
00:48:37,591 --> 00:48:39,495
Says who?

670
00:48:39,495 --> 00:48:41,617
It's just nuclear fusion.

671
00:48:44,326 --> 00:48:45,559
Look up.

672
00:48:45,559 --> 00:48:47,837
See how they sparkle?

673
00:48:47,837 --> 00:48:50,298
No need.

674
00:48:50,298 --> 00:48:54,112
Looking up won't make you lose, you know.

675
00:48:56,953 --> 00:48:59,808
It's okay to do that sometimes.

676
00:49:06,522 --> 00:49:08,210
Am I...

677
00:49:10,151 --> 00:49:13,233
shining like that, too?

678
00:49:13,233 --> 00:49:16,574
That's not very scientific.

679
00:49:16,574 --> 00:49:18,484
None of it.

680
00:49:19,160 --> 00:49:20,995
Nothing to say?

681
00:49:20,995 --> 00:49:23,789
If you were shining up there,

682
00:49:23,789 --> 00:49:27,081
you'd be undergoing nuclear fusion.

683
00:49:27,081 --> 00:49:28,742
So...

684
00:50:04,538 --> 00:50:08,069
There really are so many stars.

685
00:51:00,845 --> 00:51:02,681
A mosquito.

686
00:51:03,514 --> 00:51:05,558
A huge one.

687
00:51:05,558 --> 00:51:08,291
I saved you from a nasty bite.

688
00:51:09,019 --> 00:51:12,029
You'll freeze sleeping out here.

689
00:51:12,029 --> 00:51:14,356
Go sleep inside.

690
00:51:14,356 --> 00:51:16,189
I'll head in.

691
00:51:17,530 --> 00:51:19,269
All right...

692
00:51:38,257 --> 00:51:40,979
Why do I keep wanting to touch him?

693
00:51:46,685 --> 00:51:49,221
Get a grip, Lee Eun Chae.

694
00:52:30,557 --> 00:52:31,560
Really?

695
00:52:31,560 --> 00:52:33,103
What? Why?

696
00:52:33,103 --> 00:52:34,698
You wanted to see it.

697
00:52:40,329 --> 00:52:43,249
It's beautiful!

698
00:52:47,342 --> 00:52:49,576
The ocean!

699
00:52:52,957 --> 00:52:56,903
Does she have to scream and run like that?

700
00:52:59,215 --> 00:53:01,374
I love it here.

701
00:53:29,732 --> 00:53:32,913
<i>I love you...</i>

702
00:53:32,913 --> 00:53:35,424
<i>The wind is blowing...</i>

703
00:53:41,052 --> 00:53:43,199
[I love you]

704
00:53:47,839 --> 00:53:49,424
Can we go now?

705
00:53:51,401 --> 00:53:53,419
We just got here!

706
00:53:53,419 --> 00:53:56,287
I love it here.

707
00:53:56,287 --> 00:54:00,900
Want me to leave you in the middle of nowhere?

708
00:54:00,900 --> 00:54:03,113
That's mean!

709
00:54:16,763 --> 00:54:20,043
How does she act like that sober?

710
00:54:23,923 --> 00:54:25,883
Oh, my!

711
00:54:25,883 --> 00:54:28,556
There she goes.

712
00:54:33,420 --> 00:54:34,808
Gosh...

713
00:54:34,808 --> 00:54:38,147
Just as much trouble as I expected.

714
00:54:41,774 --> 00:54:44,088
I don't need your hand.

715
00:54:47,474 --> 00:54:48,881
Oh, my!

716
00:55:16,907 --> 00:55:19,193
Can I kiss you now?

717
00:55:22,301 --> 00:55:24,687
You're the first to ask.

718
00:56:38,223 --> 00:56:41,351
<i>I won't tell you how I feel.</i>

719
00:56:41,351 --> 00:56:42,895
<i>Why did I do that?</i>

720
00:56:42,895 --> 00:56:46,356
<i>What's with the bold lipstick all of a sudden?</i>

721
00:56:46,356 --> 00:56:49,122
<i>Don't go behind my back.</i>

722
00:56:49,122 --> 00:56:50,436
<i>Get engaged in three months.</i>

723
00:56:50,436 --> 00:56:52,196
<i>Are you playing me?</i>

724
00:56:52,196 --> 00:56:54,114
<i>Just pretend to be my fiancée.</i>

725
00:56:54,114 --> 00:56:55,532
<i>I thought...</i>

726
00:56:55,532 --> 00:56:58,214
<i>I think Tae Gyeong likes Lee Eun Chae.</i>

727
00:56:58,214 --> 00:56:59,315
<i>I smell jealousy.</i>

728
00:56:59,315 --> 00:57:00,079
<i>What?</i>

729
00:57:00,079 --> 00:57:02,830
<i>I've never been this honest in my life.</i>

730
00:57:02,830 --> 00:57:03,918
<i>Here we go again.</i>

731
00:57:03,918 --> 00:57:05,745
<i>The kissing ghost.</i>
